## VERY-IMPORTANT ##) ANSIBLE TASK EXECUTION Flow:
--------------------------------------------------

*)For every task, the control node (Ansible server) transfers the appropriate Ansible module to the managed node (remote server) through SSH. 
  The module executes locally on the managed node, collect the execution result of a module and then sends the structured result(output) to the control node, 
  and then the temporary module is removed from the manage node(remote server).

1. Read the playbook.

↓

2. Parse(Read) the current task.

↓

3. Read the module name mentioned in the task (eg: yum, shell, service, copy...)

↓

4. Load that module (eg: yum, shell, service, copy...) from the Ansible module library on the control node (or) Ansible server.

↓

5. Establish an SSH connection to the managed node (or) remote server.

↓

6. Transfer the loaded module to the managed node (or) remote server.

↓

7. Execute the module on the managed node (or) remote server.

↓

8. Collect the execution details and prepare a structured output (dictionary i.e stdout, stderr, rc, changed, failed...)

↓

9. Send output back to the control node (or) Ansible server.

↓

10. Delete the transferred temporary module (eg: yum, shell, service, copy...) from the managed node (or) remote server.

↓

11. Continue with the next task.



