##)Ansible Configuration file Precedence(preference order):
-----------------------------------------------------------

*) When you run a playbook, Ansible looks for the ansible.cfg configuration file in the following order of preference.

ANSIBLE_CONFIG( environment variable ) - First place where ansible searches for ansible.cfg
      ↓
./ansible.cfg( current directory ) - Second place where ansible searches for ansible.cfg if it is not found in 'ANSIBLE_CONFIG(environment variable)'
      ↓
~/.ansible.cfg( home directory ) - Third place where ansible searches for ansible.cfg if it is not found in './ansible.cfg( current directory)'
      ↓
/etc/ansible/ansible.cfg - Fourth place where ansible searches for ansible.cfg if it is not found in ~/.ansible.cfg( home directory)

Ansible uses the first applicable configuration file it finds.

Core Memory:

ANSIBLE_CONFIG → Current Directory → Home Directory → /etc/ansible


